# Push to GitHub after every modification

Whenever you finish modifying project source (not just analysis), sync and push to the private monorepo.

## Target

- Account: `fanqie-2580`
- Repo: https://github.com/fanqie-2580/3dnavigation (private)
- Local upload git root: `/home/ll/3dnavigation_github_upload`
- Remote: `origin` → `https://github.com/fanqie-2580/3dnavigation.git`
- Branch: `main`

## What to upload (source only)

Include changed projects under the upload root, e.g.:

- `dddmr_navigation` ← `/home/ll/dddmr_navigation` (Mid360)
- `dddmr_navigation_odin1` ← `/home/ll/dddmr_navigation_odin1` (Odin1)
- `ego-planner-swarm-ros2_version` ← `/home/ll/ego-planner-swarm-ros2_version` (Mid360)
- `ego-planner-swarm-odin1` ← `/home/ll/ego-planner-swarm-odin1` (Odin1)
- `FAST_LIO_LOCALIZATION_HUMANOID-humble` ← `/home/ll/FAST_LIO_LOCALIZATION_HUMANOID-humble`
- related packages already in the upload repo if edited

Always exclude: `build/`, `install/`, `log/`, bags (`*.bag`/`*.db3`/`*.mcap`), maps (`*.pcd`/`*.ply`), models (`*.onnx`/`*.pt`/`*.pth`/`*.engine`), large media, test dump dirs.

## Workflow after edits

1. Rsync only the touched project(s) into `/home/ll/3dnavigation_github_upload/<name>` with the exclusions above (`--copy-links`).
2. In the upload repo: `git status` / `git diff`, then commit with a concise message (why, not just what).
3. Push to `origin main` using HTTPS + Personal Access Token for `fanqie-2580` (do not use G7-3208 SSH for this repo).
4. Report the commit and repo URL to the user.

## Auth

- Do not store the PAT in git remotes or commit it.
- If push auth fails, ask the user for a `repo`-scoped PAT (or open https://github.com/settings/tokens).
- Never push secrets (`.env`, credentials, tokens).

## Exceptions

- Skip push only if the user says not to upload, or the change is analysis-only with no file edits.
- Do not force-push unless the user explicitly requests it.
